#### 3. `List<char>[]` for static symbol lookup — heap allocations + O(n) linear scan 🟡 Moderate

**Impact:** `IsSymbol` and `GetSymbolGroup` do linear scans across 5 heap-allocated `List<char>` objects. For a fixed set of ~25 characters, a `FrozenSet<char>` or a simple `bool[]` lookup table indexed by char value would be O(1).

**Files:** `Truncation.cs:L244-L250, L259-L268, L276-L287`

**Fix:** Replace with a stack-allocated or static lookup approach:

```csharp
internal static class Symbols
{
    // Flat lookup: maps char → group index (or -1)
    private static readonly FrozenDictionary<char, int> s_symbolGroupMap = BuildMap();

    private static FrozenDictionary<char, int> BuildMap()
    {
        var dict = new Dictionary<char, int>();
        ReadOnlySpan<char> g0 = ['(', ')', '[', ']', '{', '}'];
        ReadOnlySpan<char> g1 = ['+', '-', '*', '/', '=', '<', '>', '!'];
        ReadOnlySpan<char> g2 = ['.', ',', ';', ':', '?', '!'];
        ReadOnlySpan<char> g3 = ['@', '#', '$', '%', '^', '&', '~', '`'];
        ReadOnlySpan<char> g4 = ['"', '\'', '\\', '|'];
        AddGroup(dict, g0, 0); AddGroup(dict, g1, 1);
        AddGroup(dict, g2, 2); AddGroup(dict, g3, 3);
        AddGroup(dict, g4, 4);
        return dict.ToFrozenDictionary();
    }

    private static void AddGroup(Dictionary<char, int> dict, ReadOnlySpan<char> chars, int group)
    {
        foreach (char c in chars) dict[c] = group;
    }

    internal static bool IsSymbol(char c) => s_symbolGroupMap.ContainsKey(c);
    internal static int GetSymbolGroup(char c) =>
        s_symbolGroupMap.TryGetValue(c, out int g) ? g : -1;
}
```

